From 673f8a5b777e9f3e5e1506e74ff13d4c22af4e30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Forst <ensonador@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:17:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] package.json: the web/ modules are ESM

web/fm1pkg.js, web/fm1ota.js and web/bench/*.js are ES modules, and the Node tests import them from
.mjs. Without a package.json Node guesses a .js file's type, and an ambient one above the checkout
("type": "commonjs") makes the installer, syx and session tests fail on a module they cannot find a
named export in. Say it here: the tree's JavaScript is ESM. (The same patch as fm1-base's.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 package.json | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 package.json

diff --git a/package.json b/package.json
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3a239b4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package.json
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+{
+  "name": "zen-1",
+  "private": true,
+  "type": "module"
+}
-- 
